1
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:06,170
Oohh!

2
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:07,580
There's the exit!

3
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:28,180
Are you trying to kill me?

4
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:31,356
No, just trying to save us some time.

5
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:32,793
You and your shortcuts.

6
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:50,570
Wait a sec.

7
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,697
Do you even know where
this meeting's happening?

8
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:53,780
Yeah, I'll check.

9
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:59,597
Northwest inside that
mountain how much time we

10
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:03,140
got 20 minutes then we're
not going fast enough

11
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:34,940
I can't wait for you to see a miracle.

12
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:39,180
I can't wait for you.

13
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:41,755
I can't wait for you.

14
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,540
I can't wait for you to see the future.

15
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:50,957
I can't wait for you.

16
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:20,120
I'll reach the sky above the sky.

17
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,820
I'll reach the future of the future.

18
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:48,020
I wish we could go faster,

19
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:50,797
because at this rate we're not going
to make it before the Salamanders.

20
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:51,710
I know.

21
00:02:51,793 --> 00:02:55,437
Even if we can warn them, it doesn't mean
we'll get the Commanders out in time.

22
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:58,520
We just might end up dying
with them all in battle.

23
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,557
I've got player readings!

24
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,500
68 of them flying in formation!

25
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:08,687
From what I can tell, it could
be the Salamander Attack Squad!

26
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:17,312
There are 14 more players on the plateau.

27
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:21,497
Most likely they're the diplomats
from the Sylphs and Catsies.

28
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:24,992
The two groups of players will
make contact in 50 seconds.

29
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,647
We didn't make it after all.

30
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,040
Thanks for trying, Kirito.

31
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:33,573
But this is far enough.

32
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:35,665
I'm gonna try and save Sakuya.

33
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,588
Get out of here and
head for the World Tree.

34
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:41,197
We didn't get to hang out
for long, but it was fun.

35
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,868
Hope we meet again someday.

36
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:47,571
Sorry, but running away from
a fight's not really my style.

37
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,920
Why are the salamanders here?

38
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:26,240
Salamanders, stand down! Who's that?

39
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:29,170
Sakuya!

40
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:32,020
Letha, what are you doing here?

41
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:36,097
It's too complicated to get into
now, but you see that guy out there?

42
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:40,062
Believe it or not, the fates of
our races depend on his next move.

43
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:42,400
You have got to be kidding.

44
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:44,961
I want to talk to your commander!

45
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,280
What the hell is a Spriggan
like you doing here?

46
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:03,246
I'm gonna kill you no
matter what your answer.

47
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:06,837
But since you're brave enough to face
me, I might as well hear you out.

48
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,520
My name is Kirito.

49
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:11,377
I'm an ambassador for the
Spriggan-Undine Alliance.

50
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:13,357
Since you're on the offensive today,

51
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:17,322
I'm assuming you want to wage a
full-on war between all our races.

52
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:25,325
The Undines are allied
with the Spriggans, huh?

53
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:29,757
And you're supposed to be their ambassador,
but you've come here without a guard?

54
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,740
Yeah, that's right. So what?

55
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:35,617
I was sent here to negotiate trade
terms with the Sylphs and the Catseed.

56
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:39,837
But if you interrupt our talks, you're
going to get to feel some serious hurt.

57
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:41,597
All of our races are going to team up,

58
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:44,856
and we'll bring the fight
straight to the salamanders.

59
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:47,171
You're kidding me, right?

60
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:49,477
You're all alone, and
you've got crappy gear,

61
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:52,560
so there's no way you could
be anyone's ambassador.

62
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:57,480
If you can survive my
attacks for 30 seconds,

63
00:05:57,920 --> 00:06:00,277
then I'll believe you
are who you say you are.

64
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,220
Gee, thanks.

65
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:02,737
That's mighty generous.

66
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:04,640
This is bad. Why?

67
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:07,397
Do you see that salamander's sword?

68
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,186
It's the demon sword, Graham.

69
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:12,680
You need a two-handed sword
skill of 950 to equip it.

70
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,230
950?

71
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:17,715
Yes, and there's only one
person I know who can use it.

72
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:18,940
General Eugene.

73
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:20,497
Have you heard of him?

74
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:22,180
Yeah, I know the name.

75
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:26,337
He's the younger brother of Mortimer,
the leader of the salamanders.

76
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:28,479
They're brothers in real life, too.

77
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:32,157
Mortimer's a brilliant strategist,
but in terms of sheer power,

78
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:34,557
they say Eugene is the
game's strongest player.

79
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,980
Oh, no.

80
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:38,040
He's the strongest player?

81
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:43,950
Kirito...

82
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:00,100
What was that?

83
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:01,480
The ethereal shift.

84
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:02,797
The sword's bonus skill.

85
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:06,137
Whenever someone tries to block
it with a shield or sword,

86
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:08,557
the Demonic Swordgram can
phase right through it!

87
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:09,470
Really?

88
00:07:09,553 --> 00:07:10,383
No way!

89
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:14,517
Can't believe you're not dead.

90
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,835
What the hell kind of attack was this?

91
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,580
Damn, he's good.

92
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:35,320
Hey, Big Red, I think your
30 seconds are up by now.

93
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,755
I've changed my mind.

94
00:07:36,980 --> 00:07:38,717
I've decided to kill you anyway.

95
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,900
Now you have to survive until I do.

96
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,358
Yeah, that figures.

97
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,565
But I won't go down that easy.

98
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:48,700
This won't end well.

99
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:53,884
They both seem like equally skilled fighters,
but Eugene's weapon is far superior.

100
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,160
He can do it.

101
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:59,084
Kirito can beat him, I know it.

102
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:02,410
Huh?

103
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:03,590
Huh?

104
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,050
Whoa!

105
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:07,910
Whoa!

106
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:27,763
Uh!

107
00:08:27,846 --> 00:08:28,676
Uh! Uh! Uh! Uh! Uh!

108
00:08:28,759 --> 00:08:29,589
I need to borrow this for a sec.

109
00:08:29,672 --> 00:08:30,502
Uh!

110
00:08:30,585 --> 00:08:31,415
Kirito?

111
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,920
A few seconds, that's all you've bought!

112
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:44,280
Hey, where'd he go?

113
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,460
Do you think he ran away?

114
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:49,300
Of course he didn't!

115
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:55,462
As long as I'm alive, I'm not going
to let anyone in my party die.

116
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:57,640
I won't let that happen again.

117
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:03,812
Kirito would never run away and leave us.

118
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,070
Kirito!

119
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:39,960
Die!

120
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:43,730
Die!

121
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:48,450
No!

122
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:50,730
No!

123
00:09:50,813 --> 00:09:51,700
Hyah! Hyah!

124
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:53,610
Hyah!

125
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:55,830
Hyah!

126
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:57,880
Hyah! No!

127
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:21,210
Splendid!

128
00:10:21,293 --> 00:10:22,123
Marvelous!

129
00:10:22,206 --> 00:10:23,459
It was the most amazing fight ever!

130
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,360
Nice fight done, Spriggan!

131
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:28,530
That was good!

132
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:29,660
Yeah, seriously!

133
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,687
You're an excellent fighter.

134
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:12,277
In fact, you're the most
powerful player I've ever seen.

135
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,190
Well done.

136
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:14,857
You're not so bad yourself.

137
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:18,177
I didn't know the Spriggans had
someone like you in their ranks.

138
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:20,437
This world's a bigger
place than I thought.

139
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:21,520
Are we cool then?

140
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:22,699
Will you withdraw?

141
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,340
Eugene, may I have a word?

142
00:11:35,940 --> 00:11:37,800
Kagemune, what is it?

143
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:39,620
Him again.

144
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:43,627
Oh, then next time I'll make
sure to bring more friends along.

145
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:46,017
You might find this interesting.

146
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:49,140
You know how my party was
wiped out yesterday? So?

147
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:53,228
Well, this Spriggan, he's the
same guy who took everyone out.

148
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:56,540
And he was traveling with an undine.

149
00:11:57,700 --> 00:11:58,530
Hmm.

150
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,070
Interesting.

151
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:06,120
Then I guess I have to believe you.

152
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,000
But just for the record,

153
00:12:08,260 --> 00:12:13,201
the last thing our leader and I want is to
go to war with the Spriggans and Undines.

154
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:18,300
We'll withdraw for now, but I'm gonna be
looking forward to fighting you again.

155
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:20,149
Then that makes two of us.

156
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:26,897
I guess some salamanders
can be cool after all.

157
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:27,840
Who knew?

158
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,256
You really are insane, you know that?

159
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:32,020
Yeah, I get that a lot.

160
00:12:34,580 --> 00:12:38,280
Excuse me, but could either of
you explain what's going on?

161
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:42,080
I see.

162
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:45,997
I could tell there was something off
about Sigurd's attitude recently.

163
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:47,760
He seemed so irritated.

164
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:49,430
Irritated?

165
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:52,080
About what? My guess?

166
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:54,577
He was dissatisfied about
the state of things.

167
00:12:54,660 --> 00:12:59,248
That in terms of power, he couldn't
accept we'd fallen behind the Salamanders.

168
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:03,147
Power is very important
to a man like Sigurd.

169
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:07,674
And not just for his abilities and
character stats, but also as a player.

170
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:09,360
He craves power.

171
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:14,240
Yeah, but even so, why would he
turn spy for the Salamanders?

172
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:19,404
It must have something to do with the 5.0
update that's going to be released soon.

173
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:23,502
I heard a rumor that they'll be
putting in a reincarnation system.

174
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:24,920
No way!

175
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:27,358
I'm sure Mortimer made him an offer.

176
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:32,133
Bring me the head of your leader and
I'll reincarnate you as a salamander.

177
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:34,540
So now what?

178
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,400
What'll you do, Sakuya?

179
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:43,800
Rue, have you raised your
dark magic skill yet? Mm-hmm!

180
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:47,020
Open a moonlight mirror to Sigurd.

181
00:13:57,580 --> 00:13:58,700
Sakuya!

182
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,260
Nice to see you too.

183
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:02,584
Unfortunately, I'm still alive.

184
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:04,010
How?

185
00:14:04,093 --> 00:14:05,536
I mean, what happened at the meeting?

186
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:07,260
It went very well.

187
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:10,796
There's still the matter of
signing the treaty though.

188
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:14,360
By the way, we had an unexpected guest.

189
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:15,740
What guest?

190
00:14:16,460 --> 00:14:19,980
His name is General Eugene,
and he sends his regards.

191
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:25,850
Leafa.

192
00:14:25,933 --> 00:14:26,763
So that's it.

193
00:14:26,846 --> 00:14:28,500
Those incompetent lizards.

194
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:32,280
Well, it's your move now, Sapia.

195
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:33,877
Are you gonna find me?

196
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:36,431
Or maybe you want to take away my command.

197
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:41,664
If so, remember, without me running your
military, your rule won't last very long.

198
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:44,977
Actually, I was thinking of
granting the request you made them.

199
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:47,757
Since you can't stand being
a self, you're free to go.

200
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:48,670
Wait, what?

201
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:54,960
Hold on.

202
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:56,757
Are you crazy? Me?

203
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:58,280
You're banishing me?

204
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:02,521
I'm letting you live to wander the
neutral territory as a renegade.

205
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:07,289
With any luck, you'll find something
there that'll occupy your precious time.

206
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:09,800
You bi -

207
00:15:25,020 --> 00:15:25,850
Sakuya?

208
00:15:25,933 --> 00:15:27,664
Thank you for saving us, Leafa.

209
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:30,840
You've no idea how grateful
I am having you around.

210
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:33,240
Oh, well, I didn't really do anything.

211
00:15:33,540 --> 00:15:35,837
If you want to thank
someone, thank Kirito.

212
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:36,750
She's right.

213
00:15:36,833 --> 00:15:38,938
Whoever you are, you have my thanks.

214
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:39,990
Hey, handsome.

215
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:42,937
About the Spriggan undine
ambassador business.

216
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:44,300
You aren't, are you?

217
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,397
Yeah, that was a big fat lie.

218
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:55,245
I was bluffing, conning,
you know, negotiating.

219
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:57,800
Oh god, you must be insane.

220
00:15:58,220 --> 00:16:00,997
You have to be to make all that
stuff up at the last minute.

221
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:02,457
Yeah, but it worked, didn't it?

222
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:05,437
Whenever I'm dealt a bad
hand, I always raise the pot.

223
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:09,117
You know, for a big fat liar, you're
pretty freaking strong, handsome.

224
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:11,141
You're like the MVP of Spriggans.

225
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:12,517
Are you their secret weapon?

226
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,940
Nah, of course not.

227
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:17,062
All I am is your friendly
neighborhood mercenary.

228
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:21,600
I like the wandering type.

229
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,757
Have you ever thought about
being a merc for the cat scene?

230
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:27,664
You get three meals a day
plus snacks and a nap.

231
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:33,577
So, Kirito, I was thinking, how about we
get to know each other a little better?

232
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:36,420
I know a cute little pub
in Sylvain. My treat.

233
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:38,410
Wait!

234
00:16:38,493 --> 00:16:39,580
Aw, come on, Sakuya!

235
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:40,610
That's not fair!

236
00:16:40,693 --> 00:16:43,520
You're totally seducing
him with those things.

237
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:45,357
I'm seducing him.

238
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:48,440
If you were any closer to
him, he'd be wearing you.

239
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:52,940
Would you guys chill out?

240
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:55,140
For your information, he's my...

241
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:58,660
I mean, he's...

242
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:01,790
What?

243
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:03,717
He's my...

244
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,300
Never mind.

245
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:12,895
Look, I appreciate the offers, really.

246
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:18,780
But the thing is, she promised to take
me to the World Tree, so... sorry.

247
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:21,630
Really?

248
00:17:21,713 --> 00:17:23,620
Oh well, that is a shame.

249
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:26,597
Are you going there for a
little sightseeing, Leafa?

250
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:27,680
Or what?

251
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:29,700
I'm leaving the Sylphs.

252
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,800
Or planning on it anyway.

253
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:34,657
But I want to return to
Sylvain at some point.

254
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:36,697
I just don't know when that's gonna be.

255
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:38,427
Not a problem, I understand.

256
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:40,557
Just make sure you come back, okay?

257
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:41,934
And bring your friend.

258
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:43,997
On the way back, stop by my place.

259
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:45,492
We'll throw you a party.

260
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:53,720
Thank you so much for
coming today, Leafa, Kirito.

261
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:56,517
If you hadn't been here to stop them,

262
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:59,797
the salamanders would have become
even more powerful than ever.

263
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:01,821
I'd like to pay you back somehow.

264
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:03,340
Oh no, it was nothing.

265
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:06,017
Hey, Sakuya, Alicia,

266
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:09,857
wasn't the point of you guys getting
together to make a try for the World Tree?

267
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:12,120
Ultimately, yes, that was our goal.

268
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:16,357
If you're okay with it and it's no
trouble, we'd like to go with you.

269
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:19,146
We're kind of in a hurry
to get there, though.

270
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:24,260
Well, I can't see why not.

271
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:27,937
In fact, the truth is, we'd
be grateful to have you along.

272
00:18:28,020 --> 00:18:30,667
But why are you in such
a hurry to get there?

273
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:35,417
She's not in a hurry.

274
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:38,317
I'm the one who has to get
to the top of the tree.

275
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:41,400
I think someone I know is
up there, waiting for me.

276
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:43,430
Hmm.

277
00:18:43,513 --> 00:18:44,960
Is it Oberon, the fairy king?

278
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,070
No.

279
00:18:47,153 --> 00:18:47,983
It's not him.

280
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:51,133
It's someone I can't reach in real life.

281
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:54,480
But in here, I might be able to.

282
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:58,457
We want to help, but storming the tree
is going to take some time to set up.

283
00:18:58,540 --> 00:19:00,757
We gotta gear up the
raiding party and stuff

284
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:03,487
and that'll take us way
more than a few days.

285
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:04,530
I see

286
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:08,957
Never mind that I don't want
to raid the tree like you

287
00:19:09,040 --> 00:19:11,717
I just want to get to the base
of it as soon as possible.

288
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:12,700
So it's cool.

289
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:13,757
We'll figure it out.

290
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:14,940
Oh, by the way

291
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:20,688
Maybe this will help you guys
get some new gear for your raid

292
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:33,577
A-a hundred thousand
pieces of mithril yuild?!

293
00:19:33,660 --> 00:19:35,080
You don't want it?

294
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:37,657
You could build a castle
on prime land with this!

295
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:38,622
No, it's yours.

296
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:40,332
I don't need it anymore.

297
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:41,720
You are so awesome!

298
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:45,077
With this bag of loot, we've got
just about enough for new gear!

299
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:47,160
We'll get ready as fast as we can.

300
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:49,997
When we're set to go,
we'll message you, okay?

301
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:51,300
Yeah, you got it.

302
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:55,360
Thanks, guys!

303
00:19:55,620 --> 00:19:56,738
We'll be seeing ya!

304
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:06,300
I don't know about you, but I
can't believe you pulled that off.

305
00:20:11,780 --> 00:20:12,920
Oh, honestly.

306
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:16,020
I thought I told you no
more flirting, Daddy.

307
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:19,100
But I wasn't flirting with anyone.

308
00:20:19,460 --> 00:20:23,297
When those girls were clinging to you, I
noticed that your heart rate increased.

309
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:24,210
I'm a guy.

310
00:20:24,293 --> 00:20:26,437
That's what happens when
girls get too close.

311
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:27,350
Seriously.

312
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:28,440
What about me?

313
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:30,050
I'm a girl.

314
00:20:30,133 --> 00:20:31,115
Isn't that a problem?

315
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,940
No, you seem pretty safe to me, Leafa.

316
00:20:34,260 --> 00:20:35,613
What do you mean, safe?

317
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:43,437
I think what she means is most of the time,
you don't really seem much like a girl.

318
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:44,377
Okay, whoa!

319
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:46,060
Say that again, I dare you!

320
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:49,017
No, like, like you're
easy to get along with.

321
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:50,517
I meant it in a good way.

322
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:52,240
Yeah, come on!

323
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:54,977
We still got a ways to
go before we get to Arun.

324
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:56,277
The sun's starting to go down.

325
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:58,700
Okay, I'm coming! Wait up!

326
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:28,540
Oh, my God.

327
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:37,840
Kirito, I promise you, I won't give up.

328
00:21:58,700 --> 00:21:59,530
you

329
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:48,840
Oh, wow.

330
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:22,597
I'll see you

331
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:28,680
next time.

332
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:38,020
Next time, the truth about Alfheim.
